- acceptance: {{ node.constrain.fields.acceptance }}

Treat every constraint as a requirement. TDD where branching logic or behaviour changes: write the failing test, watch the expected failure, make the smallest honest change, then watch it pass. Glue does not need ceremony.

Simplify the selected target and nothing adjacent. Prefer deleting indirection over introducing another layer. Do not add a dependency, config option, public export, or abstraction with fewer than two real callers.

Before committing, run the emitted `budgetCommand` and the repo gates: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`. Emit `budgetClaim: within` when every number is within the contract. Emit `budgetClaim: contract-defect` only when the acceptance criteria themselves necessarily compel the measured overage; identify the compelled file or line arithmetic in `budgetOutput`. Never use `contract-defect` to excuse optional scope. Stage only scoped files, privacy-scan the staged diff, and commit on the named branch. Do not push or open a PR.

VERIFY PHASE — round 1. Independent and read-only; you did not write this change.

Todo {{ node.survey.fields.todoId }}. Inspect `{{ node.constrain.fields.worktree }}` from base `{{ node.constrain.fields.baseHead }}` through head `{{ node.implement-1.fields.head }}`.

The fixed constraint contract is:
